 ## Operating characteristics
-**Time Complexity:** $O(M)$ for projection of $M$ Gaussians, where each projection involves constant-time matrix operations. Sorting is $O(M \log M)$. Rasterization is $O(N \cdot K)$ where $N$ is pixels and $K$ is average splats per pixel.
-**Memory Complexity:** $O(M)$ to store projected Gaussians.
-**Performance:** Enables real-time rendering of millions of Gaussians (e.g., 134 fps on Mip-NeRF360) [S3, unofficial]. The closed-form projection avoids ray marching, which is the bottleneck in neural radiance fields.
-**Strengths:** Differentiable, fast, handles view-dependent color via SH, preserves Gaussian form locally.
-**Limitations:** The linearization approximation introduces geometric warping errors, particularly for large Gaussians or extreme FOV [S3, unofficial]. Aliasing can occur if the low-pass filter is insufficient.
